              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Salbutamol is also known as Ventolin and is primarily\nadministered by metred inhaler&nbsp;"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Salbutamol dilates the airways and stabilises the mast cells, and as such is good for asthmatic clients.&nbsp;\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Dobutamine is a beta 1 agonist that increases heart rate and increases contractility and is mainly used in the hospital setting.\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No in two ways. A chronotropic effect is one that has an effect on the heart rate (Chrono = time, like chronlolgical). But also, the word only refers to heart rate. If it increases heart rate, you would say POSITIVE chronotropic effect. In this case, the correct statement would have been \"the fact that dobutamine has a POSITIVE INOTROPIC effect means that it increases the contractility of the heart.\"&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Your answer was correct.&nbsp;A chronotropic effect is one that has an effect on the heart rate (Chrono = time, like chronlolgical). But also, the word only refers to heart rate. If it increases heart rate, you would say POSITIVE chronotropic effect. In this case, the correct statement would have been \"the fact that dobutamine has a POSITIVE INOTROPIC effect means that it increases the contractility of the heart.\"&nbsp;</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "The fact that dobutamine has a chronotropic effect tells you that it increases the contractility of the heart. \n"
                }
              ],
